-- chem/local.cub — local lower certificates on spin chains: how fast the defect of H − e₀ = Σ_patch (H_patch − e_patch)
-- falls with the patch size k. A chain H = Σ_i (J₁ S_i·S_{i+1} + J₂ S_i·S_{i+2}) is the sum over k-site patches of
-- H_k = Σ (J₁/(k−1)) S·S (neighbours) + Σ (J₂/(k−2)) S·S (next neighbours), each bond lying in k−1 patches and each
-- next-neighbour pair in k−2, so the ground energy per site is at least λ_min(H_k) (Anderson's bound): a local lower
-- certificate, checked by the inertia engine on a 2^k-dimensional patch. On states as bit lists, S_i·S_j is ¼ on equal
-- spins and −¼ on unequal ones on the diagonal, and ½ between two states that differ by exchanging spins i and j. The
-- matrices here are M = c·H_k with integers c chosen to clear denominators: Heisenberg (J₂ = 0) c = 4(k−1),
-- Majumdar–Ghosh (J₂ = J₁/2, frustration free, e₀ = −3/8 exactly) c = 16(k−1)(k−2).
import "inertiaq.cub"

